{
  "summary": "Sends the -torpassword configuration argument as a hex-encoded string in the Tor control port AUTHENTICATE command instead of a double-quoted string. It also adds a functional test verifying that passwords containing backslashes and quotes authenticate successfully against a mock Tor control server.",
  "problem": "Tor control passwords containing backslashes fail authentication or are mangled. Bitcoin Core previously sent the password as a QuotedString escaping only double quotes, causing Tor's control port parser to misinterpret backslash sequences or reject strings as unterminated.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'The Tor password was sent as a QuotedString with only double quotes escaped; as Tor interprets backslash escapes inside it, any password containing a backslash was mangled (or left the string unterminated). The Tor Control spec deliberately allows the token to be sent as unquoted hex \"to avoid escaping issues\"...'"
  ],
